WEBVTT

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:14.129
Woman: Up. Get up!

00:04:31.897 --> 00:04:35.275
Dudley: Wake up, cousin!
We're going to the zoo!

00:04:46.453 --> 00:04:51.708
Petunia: Here comes the birthday boy.
Vernon: Happy birthday, son.

00:04:53.543 --> 00:04:56.713
Cook breakfast.
And try not to burn anything.

00:04:56.963 --> 00:05:01.927
- Yes, aunt Petunia.
- I want everything to be perfect...

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:05.055
For my Dudley's special day!

00:05:05.222 --> 00:05:10.227
- Hurry up! Bring my coffee, boy.
- Yes, uncle Vernon.

00:05:11.478 --> 00:05:14.564
Petunia:
Aren't they wonderful, darling?

00:05:16.733 --> 00:05:20.237
- How many are there?
- 36. Counted them myself.

00:05:20.487 --> 00:05:23.698
36?! But last year I had 37!

00:05:23.907 --> 00:05:27.744
- But some are bigger than last year's.
- I don't care!

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:30.497
This is what we're going to do.

00:05:30.705 --> 00:05:35.085
We're going to buy you two
new presents. How's that, pumpkin?

00:05:37.045 --> 00:05:42.384
Petunia: It should be a lovely day
at the 200. I'm looking forward to it.

00:05:45.971 --> 00:05:47.764
I'm warning you now, boy.

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:51.518
Any funny business, any at all...

00:05:51.726 --> 00:05:54.771
And you won't have
any meals for a week.

00:06:04.447 --> 00:06:06.867
Dudley: Make it move.

00:06:09.536 --> 00:06:11.246
Move!

00:06:11.496 --> 00:06:13.957
- Move!
- He's asleep!

00:06:14.124 --> 00:06:16.710
He's boring.

00:06:19.129 --> 00:06:24.634
Sorry about him. He doesn't understand
what it's like, lying there...

00:06:25.093 --> 00:06:28.889
Watching people press
their ugly faces in on you.

00:06:31.641 --> 00:06:34.311
Can you hear me?

00:06:36.813 --> 00:06:40.817
It's just, I've never talked
to a snake before.

00:06:41.318 --> 00:06:42.736
Do you...?

00:06:42.944 --> 00:06:47.073
Do you talk to people often?

00:06:48.158 --> 00:06:51.494
You're from Burma, aren't you?
Was it nice there?

00:06:51.661 --> 00:06:53.997
Do you miss your family?

00:06:56.833 --> 00:07:01.588
I see. That's me as well.
I never knew my parents either.

00:07:01.796 --> 00:07:06.801
Mummy, dad, you won't believe
what this snake is doing!

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:33.536
Anytime.

00:07:36.873 --> 00:07:38.792
Man: Snake!

00:07:54.224 --> 00:07:57.602
Mum! Mummy! Help me!

00:07:57.852 --> 00:08:00.981
My darling boy!
How did you get in there?

00:08:01.481 --> 00:08:06.569
Who did this? How did you get
in there? Is there a snake?

00:08:11.408 --> 00:08:16.746
It's all right, sweetheart.
We'll get you out of these cold clothes.

00:08:18.498 --> 00:08:21.418
- What happened?
- I swear, I don't know!

00:08:21.626 --> 00:08:25.505
The glass was there
and then it was gone, like magic.

00:08:29.926 --> 00:08:32.721
There's no such thing as magic.

00:09:09.466 --> 00:09:12.177
Vernon:
Marge is ill. Ate a funny whelk.

00:09:12.385 --> 00:09:15.597
- Dad, look! Harry's got a letter!
- It's mine!
